**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The start-up import compares a catalogue's manifest hash before it reads any entry file (001 §B 'Import on every start'; 001 Summary: 'a manifest-hash comparison makes that cheap'). The catalogue seam therefore reads the manifest on its own. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/CatalogueFiles.fs`: `CatalogueProxy` (step 32) gains `readManifest : unit -> Result<CatalogueManifest, CatalogueError>` before `readCatalogue`. Its doc says that it reads and checks the manifest and opens no entry file. `createInMemory` answers the held catalogue's `manifest`, or `CatalogueIoErr` while nothing has been written, as its `readCatalogue` does. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`: `create`'s `readManifest` is the first part of `readCatalogue` in step 33's order. It reads the folder and its `.catalogue-json` (`CatalogueIoErr`) and parses the manifest with `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest` (`CatalogueFileRejectedErr`). `readCatalogue` calls it and then reads the entry files, so the two share one body. (3) On the same extension, `static member builtInFolderUnder (shipped : FolderName) : FolderName` answers the `Builtin` subfolder of `shipped`. `createBuiltInUnder` (step 81) becomes `create` over it, so `Builtin` is still written in one place; the start-up import (steps 98, 100) logs the shipped catalogue under this folder. Each doc is one line citing spec 0050 S3.1. No cache, existence check or other field is added. (4) Tests. `CatalogueProxyTests` gains `the in-memory catalogue reads its manifest alone`: before a write, `readManifest` answers `CatalogueIoErr`; after it, the written catalogue's `manifest`. `CatalogueFolderTests` gains `readManifest reads the manifest without opening an entry file`. Over a written folder, `readManifest` equals `readCatalogue`'s manifest. After one entry file is deleted, `readCatalogue` answers `MissingEntryFileErr` and `readManifest` still answers that manifest. A folder whose `.catalogue-json` was deleted answers `CatalogueIoErr`. `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given` (step 81) also checks that `builtInFolderUnder` of `Catalogue` under `System.AppContext.BaseDirectory` is its `Catalogue/Builtin` subfolder.

**Acceptance.** After the manifest read lands, `CatalogueProxy` MUST declare `readManifest`, which the folder store answers without opening an entry file; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the in-memory catalogue reads its manifest alone`, `readManifest reads the manifest without opening an entry file` and `createBuiltInUnder reads the Builtin catalogue of the shipped-catalogue folder it is given`, the count rising by 2; and build, elevation and the eleven s12 invariants MUST pass.
